  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Provision of Services in Relation to Global Pre-Departure Cultural Orientation for Australia&apos;s Refugee and Special Humanitarian Program Clients for 2019-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Cultural Orientation Programme (AUSCO) aims to empower beneficiaries with pre-departure orientation (PDO). These classes aim to enhance understanding of Australian culture and life, thereby increasing the likelihood of successful integration into their new host community. They also promote social cohesion and key Australian values over a five-day cultural orientation course. While respecting socio-cultural heterogeneity and accounting for cultural sensitivities, AUSCO ensures that programming is inclusive of all beneficiaries, including those who may be particularly vulnerable due to factors such as religion, gender, age, sexuality, or health. The programme empowers those being resettled in Australia with comprehensive information centered around key Australian values, which include respect for the freedom and dignity of the individual, freedom of religion, commitment to the rule of law, Parliamentary democracy, equality of men and women, and a spirit of egalitarianism that embraces mutual respect, tolerance, fair play, compassion for those in need, and pursuit of the public good.</narrative>
  </description>
